{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun","id":19785,"title":"Ageis Kai Doru and Mummies - brainstorming just for fun?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T09:41:29-08:00","id":19785,"title":"Ageis Kai Doru and Mummies - brainstorming just for fun?","content":"We all know that there's a very good reason why the AKD focus on Werewolves and Witches. They were written before Mummy.<br /> <br /> But what if they weren't?<br /> <br /> <br /> What history would tie them together? Would the AKD oppose mummies, just want their relics or would they have a more nuanced relationship? Does AKD trace it's origins back to Irem or did they develop their ties to the Arisen sometime later?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The more ideas the merrier. Here's some to get started:<br /> <br /> <br /> The Nameless empire never conquered prehistorical Greece, though they tried. Distance and guerilla warfare let the ancient-ancient Greeks remain independent. Being right on the fronter of the Nameless Empire the Greeks were the first to notice when the Judges ascended and the empire collapsed, their armies returned rich with spoils. The Shield and Spear began as an attempt to reverse engineer the looted Relics, to figure out the secret to their production or at least how to use them. A rather unfortunate event involving a king and a curse cut their ties to politics but thousands of years later they're still around. Their ability to create Relics is still basic, but they've gotten very good at using them and they know the best stuff can be found in a Mummy's Tomb","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T20:16:00-08:00","id":20043,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf focus was always a bit weak for AKD. I'd be inclined to just replace that with combating Mummy cults for Relics. Not that they don't ever come into conflict with Werewolves - but it's not more central to them than Vampires, Changelings, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T01:54:46-08:00","id":21061,"title":"","content":"Can you imagine the reaction to a ruthless mummy who has awakened, and decided that he has to raid the AKD's high security vaults to retrieve his whatevers? With the incredibly bombastic powers of a mummy, my thoughts are that this would need to happen exactly once to put Mummies at the top of the priority list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T02:00:14-08:00","id":21065,"title":"","content":"This thread is about alternative back-stories though; what if the earliest days of the AKD weren't influenced by Witches and Werewolves but Irem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:52:50-08:00","id":330400,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it's okay to post here, but I wonder if they might be heavily infiltrated; after all, you only need a few cultists in just the right places to ensure the &quot;true&quot; relics go to their &quot;proper&quot; owners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T12:59:21-08:00","id":330476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330400#post330400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it's okay to post here, but I wonder if they might be heavily infiltrated; after all, you only need a few cultists in just the right places to ensure the &quot;true&quot; relics go to their &quot;proper&quot; owners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the hunter organizations run off the idea that they have been infiltrated already and given the long history of the AKD, it wouldn't surprise if they've already had a few situations where that example played out and have taken measures from having it happen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:15:03-08:00","id":330490,"title":"","content":"Who says the AKD isn't the one infultrating scorpion cults and stealing their relics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:48:19-08:00","id":330662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=20043#post20043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Werewolf focus was always a bit weak for AKD. I'd be inclined to just replace that with combating Mummy cults for Relics. Not that they don't ever come into conflict with Werewolves - but it's not more central to them than Vampires, Changelings, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if you take into account the supplementary information about werewolves the focus makes more sense. Werewolves not only have fetishes (of which some are designed for anyone to use), they also make use of awakened objects (objects whose spirits are awake, so an object that can use influences and numina to aid you), ghost touched objects, and cursed items.<br /> <br /> And the differences between cursed items and relics is small enough to be declared &quot;close enough for government work,&quot; so of course aegis is going to come into conflict with a supernatural type who are also interested in relics.<br /> <br /> Now if you mean the including werewolves into the mythological origin of Aegis, yeah that's weak. Werewolves the result of a minotaur and an undead lady with bees, oookay, someone was smoking something strong there.<br /> <br /> And while the witch thing was strong in the origin story, mechanically, the coolest stuff mages make are prone to invoking paradox and becoming paper weights when the mana runs out, so it doesn't really work practically. <br /> <br /> So if you wanted to make Aegis mummy focused, replace the witches with the sorcerers of Irem. Which would make sense mythologically and practically. Sorcerers make relics, Aegis collects relics and pine for the old days in which they had the secrets of Irem at their fingerprints, and you know Aegis being survivors of the Shiantu (or however it's spelled) slaughtering everyone would give them a good strong basis for their grudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 12-04-2014, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T19:44:24-08:00","id":330719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330662#post330662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you wanted to make Aegis mummy focused, replace the witches with the sorcerers of Irem. Which would make sense mythologically and practically. Sorcerers make relics, Aegis collects relics and pine for the old days in which they had the secrets of Irem at their fingerprints, and you know Aegis being survivors of the Shiantu (or however it's spelled) slaughtering everyone would give them a good strong basis for their grudge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the Cult of the Phoenix/Cult of Seth would be more interesting to tie in. They both have roots in egypt and most likely came from Iramic roots in their past. AKD seem to have a more of a Greek culture to it with it's emphasis on labyrinths and it's HQ in Athens which somewhat implies that it came later.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:44:45-08:00","id":330742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330719#post330719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the Cult of the Phoenix/Cult of Seth would be more interesting to tie in. They both have roots in egypt and most likely came from Iramic roots in their past. AKD seem to have a more of a Greek culture to it with it's emphasis on labyrinths and it's HQ in Athens which somewhat implies that it came later.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> See Mortal Remains for more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T22:11:47-08:00","id":330762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330742#post330742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.<br /> <br /> See Mortal Remains for more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the book on PDF but I have to admit, it comes with certain flaws at a few things.<br /> <br /> But going back to the purpose of the thread which is to find a way to combine the AKD and Irem, I would mostly put them firmly after Arisen were created and scattered throughout the world and just one of those mortal organizations that arose after a few turns, got very clued on on relics and the Arisen, and have fought with them throughout the ages.<br /> <br /> Mostly like it because it's a clash of mummy vs an eternal idea. One that keeps reforming over time and no matter how many times you bash it over the head, it adapts and survives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T04:59:29-08:00","id":330987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330662#post330662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if you mean the including werewolves into the mythological origin of Aegis, yeah that's weak.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct - this thread is about the mythological / historical origin of Aegis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330719#post330719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the Cult of the Phoenix/Cult of Seth would be more interesting to tie in. They both have roots in egypt and most likely came from Iramic roots in their past. AKD seem to have a more of a Greek culture to it with it's emphasis on labyrinths and it's HQ in Athens which somewhat implies that it came later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it has to be just one or the other?<br /> <br /> The Ascending Ones have a shared background in Egyptian myth, and there's a lot of cool mileage in the Ascending Ones as the protectors of the down trodden vs cults recruiting from the downtrodden. The Ascending One's MO of stealth and assassination also makes them well suited to taking out high priests and sowing chaos in a cult that's too large for open warfare or a cult led by a mummy who'll go old testiment if hunters started fighting his cultists.<br /> <br /> The Ageis Kai Doru have a shared interest in relics, and there's a lot of cool mileage in the AKD and Mummy cults both being large secretive organisations with very long term conflicting occult plans and fingers in corridors of power. The Ageis Kai Doru's possession of uberpowerful relics also makes them well suited to actually fighting a Mummy head on.<br /> <br /> IMO both Conspiracies work great against Mummies for entirely different reasons. There's no need to talk about which one is better suited. This thread is about AKD/Mummies, but if you want to start a thread about Ascending Ones &amp; Mummies there's lots of great material to cover there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T07:18:44-08:00","id":331057,"title":"","content":"Lore wise, it is easy to tie something like the AKD to any supernatural splat. Mummies make as much sense as say Vampires, but sure, I'll bite. Mummies and AKD could be splinters of Irem, Mummies being the chosen of the culture, the AKD being the servants and slaves who survived the culture's collapse. Sure, the story has changed over time, but Mummies from the century near the fall of Irem might remember the &quot;shield and spear&quot; rebellions, when the teeming slave masses rose up against the mages and masters of Irem. It has been millinia since then, and human memories are only so finite, the AKD my only have vague memories of their beginnings, but the Mummies may remember them <i>very</i> well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T20:12:36-08:00","id":333696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/19785-ageis-kai-doru-and-mummies-brainstorming-just-for-fun?p=330719#post330719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the Cult of the Phoenix/Cult of Seth would be more interesting to tie in. They both have roots in egypt and most likely came from Iramic roots in their past. AKD seem to have a more of a Greek culture to it with it's emphasis on labyrinths and it's HQ in Athens which somewhat implies that it came later.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Nameless Empire included Asia Minor, which was conquered by Alexander the Great and the Levant, which has had greeks in it for 4000 years, and since the mummies treat Irem like a proto-culture with a global legacy, the Aegis could have Iremite origins and been Greek even earlier than that. I'd say several thousand years is plenty of time to absorb cultural affectations.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I'm a minority opinion, but replacing a grandiose origin myth (We predate werewolves, and come from a city that never existed!) with &quot;We come from an Egyptian cult that wasn't particularly important&quot; seems like a bigger change than even replacing witches or werewolves with mummies.<br /> <br /> So keeping the tone I'd go for &quot;We were the guardians of the greatest city that ever existed, the crown jewel of an empire so great it needed no name, crafted by magic and war. But then it fell, betrayed by our own god-kings. We scattered to the four winds, in our exile we were attacked by savage feral creatures who envied our magic for themselves. But we remember, we are the inheritors of great magic and of the greatest civilization that ever lived, and we will never forget the debts of blood we owe to both the witches who betrayed us and the werewolves who attacked us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I thought I'd point out that I feel that this mythical origin isn't factual, but embellished. The 42's honor guard, maybe a handful of them fled instead of getting sacrificed, but hardly enough to form a global conspiracy. Far more likely, using this mythical origin as a basis, the proto-Aegis were the army of the nameless empire, after the empire fell because the 42 sacrificed the entire capital city, the army changed from cannon fodder to the guys with fighting abilities and magical weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 12-08-2014, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}